  "practice": [
    "Say the historical ঞ sound roughly like ny or ñ, similar to the middle of canyon. In everyday Bangla, learn its conjunct forms and whole words.",
    "Recognize the most important shapes: ঞ্চ, ঞ্ছ, ঞ্জ, and ঞ্ঝ. ঞ almost never appears alone at the beginning of everyday words.",
    "Practice ঞ্চ = ঞ্ + চ in পাঁচ, পঞ্চাশ, পঞ্চম, অঞ্চল, সঞ্চয়, and মঞ্চ.",
    "Practice ঞ্জ = ঞ্ + জ in অঞ্জলি, গঞ্জ, কুঞ্জ, ব্যঞ্জন, রঞ্জন, and মঞ্জুর.",
    "Compare ঙ, associated with ng in আঙুল and ভাঙা, with ঞ, usually hidden inside conjuncts in পাঁচ, অঞ্চল, সঞ্চয়, and মঞ্চ.",
    "Use পাঁচ, পঞ্চাশ, পঞ্চম, অঞ্চল, সঞ্চয়, মঞ্চ, বঞ্চিত, and ব্যঞ্জন as quick reading anchors.",
    "Recognize these phrases instantly: পাঁচ মিনিট, পাঁচ দিন, পঞ্চাশ টাকা, টাকা সঞ্চয় করো, and মঞ্চে যাও."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "ঞ is a Bangla consonant historically associated with a ny or ñ sound. It almost never appears by itself at the beginning of everyday words.",
    "The best way to learn ঞ is by recognizing it inside conjunct letters, especially ঞ্চ, ঞ্ছ, ঞ্জ, and ঞ্ঝ.",
    "গঞ্জ commonly appears in Bangladeshi place names and historically refers to a market town or trading place.",
    "Do not confuse ঞ with ঙ: ঙ is associated with ng, while ঞ is usually hidden inside conjuncts such as ঞ্চ and ঞ্জ.",
    "Best words to memorize include পাঁচ, পঞ্চাশ, পঞ্চম, অঞ্চল, আঞ্চলিক, সঞ্চয়, সঞ্চিত, সঞ্চালন, মঞ্চ, বঞ্চিত, বঞ্চনা, লাঞ্ছনা, অঞ্জলি, গঞ্জ, ব্যঞ্জন, and ব্যঞ্জনবর্ণ."
  ]
